<title>USA: Exec cuts Centennial Cellular stake.</title>
<headline>Exec cuts Centennial Cellular stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>George Schrenk, chief executive of Comp Comm Inc, said Monday he reduced his stake in Centennial Celluar Corp to 4.91 percent or 453,900 common shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission Schrenk said he sold 34,500 shares of Centennial on July 2 and 3. He did not specify how much he received for the shares.</p>
<p>Schrenk said he holds the stake in Centennial for investment.</p>
</text>
